If you haven't been to hell, the following may spoil you.

Joyously was I cruising when I came apon a maze.  Having failed in discovering
a down-staircase I was enlightened by a writer from rec.games.hack that I
required a teleport.  Nimbly I ran up two levels, jumped into a level
transporter and went to hell.

I slashed, I hacked, I mutilated those foul creatures of evil, till I came 
across a body...but it was no ordinary body, for t'was a body of water.

T'was square, with no way over.  Dispatching a nearby chameleon revealed a ring
of levitation...it's time of appearance impeccible.  Putting it on, I gently
floated over the pool and came apon a wall.  Choosing my favorite pick-axe,
I clobberred the wall with a mighty heave, sending shards of rock to the far
reaches of the world.

Came rushing forth a Demon Prince accompanied by hounds of hell.  But I had
the speed and the heroism, and dutifully dispatched them to a lower dimension.

Clambering inside, my heart leapt in joy.  The Amulet!  I'd found it!

Rushing back to yonder stair, I did not pause to explore.  I began my run, a 
speedy ascent back to the mouth of the dungeon.

Through hordes of monsters did I wade, my crysknife slashing wide and deep.
T'was not till 13 levels from the top did I happen apon a scroll of identify.

Carefully I read the runes, and aimed my focus apon amulet....

N) A cheap plastic imitation of the amulet of Yendor.

I stood in shock for time unknown, then came forth a mighty roar that echoed
through the dungeon and awoke the Wizard himself....

DOH!

